title: MeetingNiko
---
<<declare $playerName = "player">>
<<gatherVars>>
<<declare $NikoImage = false>>

When you entered the library, the smell of new books and warm
coffee washed over you. The murmurs of students studying filled
the room. The library was always cozy, a place you liked to
study and read assigned books.

A good candidate for this essay would definitely be here, you
thought. Bookworms could have the best opinions on life. You
looked around for the right person to ask.

You: "This is impossible,"

You sighed. Everyone was in groups, studying or chatting. You
felt too awkward approaching a group to ask about your
questionnaire.

Turning to a bookcase, you shrugged and scanned the shelves.
Nothing caught your interest, and that's when you turned your
head.

To your right stood a lone man dressed in blacks and browns,
like a character from a gothic novel. The only bright features
were the blonde highlights in his hair and his amber eyes as
they scanned the books.

His hands brushed the spines delicately before stopping and
selecting one with precision. He opened it one-handed and read
a few pages before nodding.

Then he turned, meeting your gaze with piercing eyes.

Startled, you quickly looked away, your face warming with
embarrassment. You heard him sigh.

<<set $NikoImage to true>>
Niko: "Do you need something?"
<<set $NikoImage to false>>

His voice was gravelly and rough, laced with annoyance. You
didn't want to bother him, but you needed a candidate. Maybe
approaching a group would have been easier.

-> walk away
    <<jump WalkAway>>

-> freeze up
    <<jump FreezeUp>>

-> walk towards him
    <<jump WalkTowardsHim>>
===

title: WalkAway
---
You decide you can't do it and quickly try to leave. You don't
notice the pile of books on the floor and trip.

You hit the ground with a loud thud.

Embarrassed, you scramble up, trying to escape.

<<set $NikoImage to true>>
Niko: "That looked like it hurt,"
<<set $NikoImage to false>>

He laughs mockingly, making your face burn. You've never felt
more humiliated.

He watches you with a wide smile, clearly amused.

Swallowing your pride, you approach him anyway. His eyebrow
raises at your boldness.

You: "Hi, my name is {$playerName}. I need volunteers for my
last essay in Philosophy,"

You: "and I was wondering if you'd be interested in being one?"

You gather what confidence you can. He responds with an amused
smile.

<<jump MeetingNiko2>>
===

title: FreezeUp
---
You: "Uhh..."

A terrible start. You sigh internally.

He looks down at you with quiet confidence, which irritates
you. Still, you push forward.

You: "Hi, my name is {$playerName}. I need volunteers for my
last essay in Philosophy,"

You: "and I was wondering if you'd be interested in being one,"

You explain your purpose as confidently as possible. He only
raises an eyebrow.

<<jump MeetingNiko2>>
===

title: WalkTowardsHim
---
You gather your confidence and approach him. He raises an
eyebrow as you near.

He turns fully to face you, towering over you. His eyes seem to
glow under the shadows, and he looks more annoyed than curious.

You begin to regret interrupting him.

You: "Hi, my name is {$playerName}. I need volunteers for my
last essay in Philosophy,"

You: "and I was wondering if you'd be interested in being one,"

You state your case. He responds with a soft scoff.

<<jump MeetingNiko2>>
===

title: MeetingNiko2
---
He closes his eyes briefly, thinking, then sighs.

When he opens them, his expression softens.

<<set $NikoImage to true>>
Niko: "Okay,"
<<set $NikoImage to false>>

He sounds content.

<<set $NikoImage to true>>
Niko: "I agree to volunteer for your candidates,"
<<set $NikoImage to false>>

He seems more approachable now, his guard lowered. Whatever you
said convinced him.

He shifts and faces you fully. The tension around him fades.

You notice a satchel on his shoulder and the book he holds.

The book is gold-lined, titled "Wuthering Heights."

<<set $NikoImage to true>>
Niko: "My name is Niko. I'm studying Music. Nice to meet you,"
<<set $NikoImage to false>>

He extends his hand. You hesitate before shaking it.

His hand is cold, and he pulls away quickly, grimacing.

You: "It's nice to meet you too,"

You give him your first question. He looks confused, but after
your explanation, he nods slowly.

<<set $NikoImage to true>>
Niko: "I'll answer this tomorrow...goodbye for now,"
<<set $NikoImage to false>>

Just like that, he dismisses you and walks away.

You watch him go, unsure what to think.

-> Like him
    <<jump EndingPart>>

-> Don't mind him
    <<jump EndingPart>>

-> Don't like him
    <<jump EndingPart>>
===

title: EndingPart
---
You've got a candidate sorted. No need to stay any longer.

Time to head home...
===